  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In the given circuit the input voltage <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>in</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msub></math> is shown in figure. The cut-in voltage of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi></math> junction diode (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>) is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>. Which of the following output voltage <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfenced></math> waveform across the diode is correct?</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/5d75a0e0-485c-4ea1-972d-5e4d5fa8257f-image.png\" style=\"width: 560px; height: 142px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
